{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1736,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He robbed twenty-eight stagecoaches, and he was finally caught by his laundry.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 93
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Meet Black Bart. A sack over his head, a shotgun he never fired.",
   "from": 97,
   "to": 195
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "bart",
   "text": "Throw down the box, please.",
   "from": 198,
   "to": 256
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He took the strongbox, left a poem, and vanished into the hills.",
   "from": 259,
   "to": 365
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Nobody ever saw his face. Detectives James Hume and Harry Morse had nothing.",
   "from": 369,
   "to": 472
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "hume",
   "text": "No name, no face, no trail.",
   "from": 475,
   "to": 537
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Because by day, Black Bart was Charles Bolton, a gentleman in mining with fine white shirts.",
   "from": 540,
   "to": 675
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then, in eighteen eighty-three, a young man by the road fires at the running bandit.",
   "from": 679,
   "to": 797
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Bart is barely grazed. But in the bushes, he leaves something behind. A handkerchief.",
   "from": 801,
   "to": 919
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In one corner, four tiny marks. F, X, O, seven.",
   "from": 923,
   "to": 1028
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, every city laundry stamped its own code on your linen, so your shirts came back to you.",
   "from": 1044,
   "to": 1168
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And each laundry kept a book. Code on one side, customer on the other.",
   "from": 1171,
   "to": 1262
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So the detectives carried one handkerchief from laundry to laundry.",
   "from": 1266,
   "to": 1349
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "laundryman",
   "text": "F, X, O, seven? That's Mister Bolton. Very clean man.",
   "from": 1352,
   "to": 1445
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The detectives knock on the gentleman's door.",
   "from": 1449,
   "to": 1501
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "morse",
   "text": "Good morning, Mister Bolton. Or should we say, Bart?",
   "from": 1504,
   "to": 1610
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Twenty-eight robberies without a single shot, undone by one dirty handkerchief.",
   "from": 1614,
   "to": 1712
  }
 ],
